# No tar-ignore for crates/target/ here on purpose. dpkg-source's
# --tar-ignore (used for "3.0 (native)" format instead of --diff-ignore,
# which only affects non-native diffs) matches path components anywhere in
# the tree, not just at the source root — a "target"-named pattern would
# also strip any vendor/*/src/target/ subdirectory some vendored crate
# happens to ship (not confirmed present today, but not worth the risk).
# Instead, debian/scripts/prepare-offline-build.sh removes crates/target/
# outright before packaging — see docs/LAUNCHPAD.md.
